sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Asha (browser)
    participant B as Ravi (browser)
    participant API as JoinService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over A,B: 1 seat left, both tap Join at the same moment
    par
        A->>API: POST /activities/42/join<br/>Idempotency-Key: k1
    and
        B->>API: POST /activities/42/join<br/>Idempotency-Key: k2
    end
    API->>DB: BEGIN, INSERT idempotency_keys (user, k1)
    API->>DB: BEGIN, INSERT idempotency_keys (user, k2)
    API->>DB: (Asha) UPDATE activities SET seats_taken = seats_taken + 1<br/>WHERE id = 42 AND status = 'OPEN' AND seats_taken + 1 <= capacity
    API->>DB: (Ravi) the same UPDATE
    Note right of DB: Ravi's UPDATE waits on the row lock,<br/>then re-checks the WHERE on the new row
    DB-->>API: 1 row updated (Asha)
    API->>DB: INSERT participant, ledger +1, outbox ParticipantJoined, COMMIT
    API-->>A: 200 JOINED, seatsLeft 0
    DB-->>API: 0 rows updated (Ravi)
    API->>DB: INSERT waitlist (position), outbox, COMMIT
    API-->>B: 200 WAITLISTED, position 1
    Note over A,DB: Asha retries after a timeout with k1: the saved response is replayed, no second seat
